{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>There is no soundness</b> — from the root תם. The meaning is health. And he mentioned the proximate cause of this — because of Your wrath — and the remote cause." "<b>Because of my sin</b> — for on its account You were wrathful with me."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {0 "Reading הסבה הקרובה למה זה as 'the proximate cause of this'; the phrase למה זה may alternatively mean 'for what reason this is', making the syntax slightly awkward."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:06.272127636Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}